@startuml seq_com_bus_off
title SC-COM-04 - Bus-off of the TCU over the full CAN path

participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "can0 / slcand\n(Pi5, SocketCAN)" as Can0
participant "Gateway\n(FRDM-MCXN236)" as GW
participant "CAN bus\n500 kbit/s" as Bus
participant "TCU" as TCU
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over Plant, LED
Covers: SYS-COM-006, SYS-COM-002, SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-003, SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-008, SYS-FLT-001, SYS-HMI-001,
SIM-GW-001, SIM-GW-003, SIM-PLT-004, SG-04
The gateway forwards every frame in both directions without filtering or changing it (DC-05, SIM-GW-001).
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> Can0 : SIM_Driver, SIM_Speed, SIM_Analog
  Can0 -> GW : SLCAN frames over USB VCOM
  GW -> Bus : CAN frames 0x100 .. 0x102
  Bus -> TCU : 0x100 .. 0x102
  TCU -> Bus : TCU_Actuators 0x200
  Bus -> GW : 0x200
  GW -> Can0 : SLCAN frame
  Can0 -> Plant : TCU_Actuators
end

== t0: bus failure (e.g. CANH / CANL shorted, SYS-COM-006 verification) ==
Bus ->x TCU : frames lost
TCU -> TCU : t0: bus-off; try to recover (SYS-COM-006)
note right of TCU: during the failure the TCU neither transmits\nnor receives
GW -> Can0 : SLCAN status flags: error passive / bus-off (SIM-GW-003)
GW -> GW : bus-off shown on a board LED (SIM-GW-003)
alt bus back within 30 ms
  TCU -> TCU : recovered; no reception timeout, no fault
  TCU -> Bus : TCU_Actuators 0x200 (normal outputs)
  note right of TCU: the plant receives TCU_Actuators again\nbefore its 50 ms timeout (SIM-PLT-004)
else bus not back within 30 ms
  TCU -> TCU : t0 + 30 ms: no SIM_Driver, SIM_Speed, SIM_Analog -> communication faults\n(FaultBits 7, 8, 9) (SYS-COM-002) -> enter limp-home, latched (SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-004)
  TCU -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
  note right of TCU: the limp-home outputs cannot be transmitted\nwithin 100 ms during bus-off\n(open question N-06 in system_design.md)
  ... 50 ms without TCU_Actuators ...
  Plant -> Plant : t0 + 50 ms: hydraulic default (SIM-PLT-004):\nsame gear (3rd in D) and pressure as limp-home (SYS-FLT-003 note)
  alt bus back within 1000 ms
    TCU -> TCU : recovered; no bus-off fault (SYS-COM-006)
  else bus not back within 1000 ms
    TCU -> TCU : t0 + 1000 ms: bus-off fault (FaultBits 10, DTC U0001-88) (SYS-COM-006);\ncontinue to try to recover
    TCU -> LED : ON within 100 ms after the bus-off fault is set (SYS-FLT-003);\nhere already ON from the communication faults
    ... bus available again ...
  end
  TCU -> Bus : TCU_Actuators 0x200: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, FaultLamp = ON
  note right of TCU: limp-home outputs as soon as\nthe bus is available again (SYS-FLT-003)
  TCU -> Bus : TCU_Status 0x201: Mode = 1 (Limp-home), FaultBits 7, 8, 9 (and 10) = 1
  note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-04: limp-home, latched; the fault bits stay set until the next power cycle (SYS-FLT-008).
end
Bus -> GW : 0x200, 0x201
GW -> Can0 : SLCAN frames
Can0 -> Plant : TCU_Actuators
Plant -> Plant : uses TCU_Actuators again
@enduml
